= Treaty of Rapallo

**<span style="color: #000;">Ge</span><span style="color: #D00;">rma</span><span style="color: #FC0;">ny</span>** and the **<span style="color: #CD0000;">Soviet Union</span>**, both diplomatically isolated and economically ruined, meets at Rapallo.

The two powers has reached an agreement of renouncing all territorial claim, and financial claim against each other and opened friendly diplomatic relation, mutual diplomatic recognition and pledging to increase economic ties among each other.

- @consequence

@consequence
title: What does it mean for Poland?
on-arrival: instability += 1; president_confidence -= 10

The populace is threatened for the two territorial powers to its west and east has reconciled.

Piłsudski's confidence in the republic has waned in fear of a new partition.
